#
# The fuzz seed corpus is bytes, not text.
#
# Every one of those files is a `.nbin` whose exact contents are the test, and
# three of them exist precisely because one byte in them is wrong. Any line
# ending normalisation on the way in or out of the repository would rewrite a
# 0x0d 0x0a pair somewhere inside a shape vector and turn a seed into a
# different seed, silently. Marking them binary is what stops that, and it also
# keeps `git diff` from trying to print them.

*.nbin binary
fuzz/corpus/** binary
